No toast library found in the codebase. Here's the research.

## 1. Toast library — not present

No toast/notistack/sonner library exists. `frontend/package.json` dependencies contain no toast package (only `@radix-ui/react-tooltip`, `lucide-react`, `recharts`, etc.). A grep for `toast|Toast|sonner|react-hot-toast|notistack` across the whole frontend returned zero matches. There is no `toast.info(...)` pattern anywhere, and no `Toaster`/`Provider` mounted in any layout. **If you want a toast, you'd need to add a library and mount its Provider — nothing exists to reuse.**

## 2. Inline info banner/alert component

None found — no dedicated banner/alert component exists in `frontend/components` (searched for banner/alert/tip patterns; only `Tooltip.tsx`, `Tag`, etc. turned up as UI primitives in the header). You'd be building a new inline banner element from scratch (e.g., a `<div>` with icon + text using existing Tailwind classes), not reusing an existing component.

## 3. `frontend/components/Tooltip.tsx` — reusable for a "?" icon

Yes, directly reusable. Key props (lines 7-17):
```ts
interface TooltipProps {
  label?: string;
  content: ReactNode;
  showArrow?: boolean;
  showQuestionMark?: boolean;      // default true — renders the "?" icon button
  triggerMode?: "hover" | "click" | "pageload";
  className?: string;
  style?: CSSProperties;
  children?: ReactNode;
  childrenClassName?: string;
}
```
Default usage (no `children`) renders a standalone "?" icon button that shows `content` on hover — perfect next to a heading. Example from the same page (lines 169-181) shows the alternate pattern (wrapping `children`, `showQuestionMark={false}`), but omitting `children` gives you the bare question-mark icon trigger with default `showQuestionMark=true`. So: `<Tooltip content="沒有詳細的課程進度資訊" triggerMode="hover" />` next to the `<h1>` would work with zero new code.

## 4. Header JSX structure — `frontend/app/course/[courseKey]/page.tsx` lines 163-222

The `<h1>` with `courseDetail?.course_name` is at line 190-192, inside a `flex flex-col gap-2` div (line 189) that also holds the Tag row:
```tsx
189  <div className="flex flex-col gap-2">
190    <h1 className="headline-1-sb text-gray-90 flex items-center gap-2">
191      {courseDetail?.course_name}
192    </h1>
193    <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
...tags...
209    </div>
210  </div>
```
The `<h1>` already has `flex items-center gap-2` — a `<Tooltip>` "?" icon can be dropped inside the `<h1>` right after `{courseDetail?.course_name}` (still line 191) without disrupting layout, since flex + gap-2 already accommodates an inline sibling. Alternatively, a full banner could be inserted as a new sibling `<div>` right after line 210 (closing the `flex flex-col gap-2` block) and before line 211 (the closing `</div>` of the `space-y-2` wrapper at line 167), spanning full width beneath the tags, still inside `<header>` (closes line 222).
